# Wrangler reads this from the assets directory (= repo root, per the registry deploy entry).
# Everything NOT excluded here is published on the client's live business domain.
#
# This list is deny-by-pattern and has already failed once by being too narrow: it was written
# after DEPLOY.md leaked, so it covered *.md and nothing else — and ROOM.json, which matched no
# pattern, was merged straight past it. Add the file type, not just the filename that bit you.
#
# After EVERY deploy, confirm nothing internal is reachable:
#   for f in DEPLOY.md ROOM.json BRIEF.md; do
#     curl -s -o /dev/null -w "$f %{http_code}\n" "https://www.oudkempeneetcafe.nl/$f"; done
#   → every one must be 404.
*.md
*.json
*.sql
*.py
*.toml
.assetsignore
.gitignore
.github/
data/
migrations/
tools/
tests/
